# Keep every byte exactly as committed.
#
# Why this file exists: this repo ships a sha256.txt manifest so users can verify that the
# files they received are the ones we published. Any git-side line-ending conversion would
# silently break that check -- a single checkout turning LF into CRLF makes every hash
# mismatch, and the failure looks like "the download was tampered with".
#
# The tree is deliberately mixed today (docs are LF, install.ps1 and install.cmd are CRLF),
# so we do NOT normalise: `-text` tells git to store and check out files verbatim.
* -text

# Binaries (declared explicitly so they are never diffed as text)
*.ico binary
